    "title": "Custom Ford Roadster Pickup at No Reserve",
    "summary": "This 1931 Ford Model A was transformed into a hot rod built around a 1927 Model T pickup body, a 1931 Model A frame, and a modified 201ci Ford inline-four. The engine uses a Thomas aluminum head, 6.7:1 compression ratio, a 3/4 race camshaft, bronze timing gear, a Stromberg 97 carburetor, aluminum downdraft intake, tubular headers, and a '43 Ford GPW Autolite distributor. The frame was Z'd and lowered six inches in front, lengthened four inches in the rear, and fitted with split wishbones. Four-wheel '39 Ford hydraulic drum brakes, a modified '40 Ford V8 clutch, 12-volt electrical system, wire wheels, and a three-speed manual transmission complete the build. The seller states that the project was started in California, completed in 2002, and donated to the Motorsports Hall of Fame of America in Daytona Beach in 2007. The seller purchased the car in July 2021. This Model A is now offered at no reserve with a three-binder notebook documenting the build and a Florida title in the seller's name listing the car as a 1931 Ford convertible.",
